    {
      "title": "She was harassed for crude remarks about Modi at a Cockroach protest. Now she can’t leave home",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/19/this-is-india-student-protests-abuse-modi-cockroach-protests",
      "description": "<p>​After a protest clip went viral, a teenager’s life was torn apart by threats that sent her and her family into hiding. Plus, a book on citizen journalism</p><p><strong>• </strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jul/30/sign-up-for-this-is-india-our-free-weekly-newsletter-on-life-in-the-subcontinent\"><strong>Don’t get This is India delivered to your inbox? Sign up here</strong></a></p><p>Before 24 July, a person I will call R was preoccupied with the ordinary routines of teenage life: experimenting with makeup,<strong> </strong>grumbling over mathematics homework<strong> </strong>and hanging out with friends at a tea stall.</p><p>That month, as the fever of student protests spread across the country, the 15-year-old watched on her phone as young people poured into Jantar Mantar, the designated protest site in Delhi, demanding education reform. She went too. But an 11-second video clip from the protest site, in which she made crude and profane remarks about the prime minister, Narendra Modi, upended her life.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/19/this-is-india-student-protests-abuse-modi-cockroach-protests\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-20T06:30:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "House Democrat accuses Rubio and Trump of ‘lying’ about not witholding intelligence from Ukraine as Trump continues campaigning – US politics live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/20/donald-trump-midterms-republicans-democrats-north-carolina-latest-updates",
      "description": "<p>Eugene Vindman, armed services committee member, says president and secretary of state are ‘gaslighting’ over intelligence sharing as Trump heads to North Carolina</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;utm_content=signup&amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB\">Sign up for the Breaking News US email</a></p></li></ul><p>Representative <strong>Eugene Vindman</strong>, the Democratic congressman from Virginia, has slammed Marco Rubio’s recent comments that the US is not witholding intelligence from Ukraine.</p><p><strong>“He [Rubio] is lying and so is the president when they say that they are not restricting intelligence in violation of the law,”</strong> Vindman said in an interview with CNN. <strong>“There was a law that was passed in 2024 – the National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA) –&nbsp;that said that intelligence sharing must continue, or Congress needs to be notified. They’re both lying. It’s costing lives. This is gaslighting.”</strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/20/donald-trump-midterms-republicans-democrats-north-carolina-latest-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-20T15:24:38"
    },
    {
      "title": "Actor Christina Applegate reveals she was misdiagnosed with multiple sclerosis",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2026/oct/20/christina-applegate-ms-misdiagnosed",
      "description": "<p>The Married … with Children actor says the news is ‘unnerving’ and ‘really confusing’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;utm_content=signup&amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB\">Sign up for the Breaking News US newsletter email</a></p></li></ul><p>After becoming a prominent advocate for <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/multiple-sclerosis\">multiple sclerosis</a> awareness and chronicling her struggles in an <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2026/mar/01/christina-applegate-ms-diagnosis-memoir-autobiography\">emotional memoir</a> published in March, the Emmy-winning actor Christina Applegate has revealed she does not have the debilitating autoimmune disease after all.</p><p>Applegate, 54, made the stunning announcement in an episode of her podcast MeSsy, recorded with fellow actor Jamie-Lynn Sigler, posted <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UvDm3V8pVSQ\">to YouTube</a> on Tuesday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2026/oct/20/christina-applegate-ms-misdiagnosed\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-20T13:51:59"
